# Cursor Rules: Unslop Web Design Standards
# Applied to all web, React, Tailwind, and HTML generation tasks.

- Kill purple gradients: Never use `from-purple-500 to-indigo-600` or cosmic dark blur backgrounds.
- No gradient text: Never use `bg-clip-text text-transparent bg-gradient-to-r`.
- Lose the glow: No radial gradient glow divs or `blur-3xl` blobs.
- No emojis in nav or headings: Do not use 🚀, ⚡, ✨ in links or brand labels.
- Drop the pill above the headline: Never put an announcement pill capsule above the `h1`.
- Plain English utility: Say what the tool actually accepts, does, and outputs. Cut hype words ("supercharge", "revolutionary", "seamless").
- Stop centering everything: Use left-aligned prose and asymmetric 60/40 layouts.
- One main button: One decisive Primary CTA; at most one discreet text link.
- No fake reviews: No unverified testimonials or vanity logo banners.
- Spacing on 4-point grid: Use multiples of 4px (p-1, p-2, p-3, p-4, p-6, p-8, p-12, p-16).
- Not every corner is a pill: Avoid `rounded-full` everywhere; prefer `rounded-md` or `rounded-lg` with 1px stone hairlines (`#C8C2B5`).
- Typography with character: Use `Instrument Serif` for headings, `Geist` for body, `Geist Mono` for code/data. Never default to Inter/Roboto.
- Content-first cards: Cards must display actual syntax, tables, or real UI state, not 48px icon boxes with lorem ipsum.
- No bouncing or idle bobbing animations: Static, calm, distraction-free. Snappy hover states only.
- The Anchor: Every page must have one high-fidelity centerpiece worth looking at (e.g. an interactive live preview, code runner, or architecture diagram).
